  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAs">IV As</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q">Et item, ne dominus libero homini hlafordsocnam prohibeat, qui ei per omnia rectum fecerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#attenborough" n="5" corresp="#wit-q">[Ne dominus libero homini ius prohibeat.] [Q/Br] Et item, ne dominus libero homini hlafordsocnam prohibeat, qui ei per omnia rectum fecerit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-q">And further, a freeman who has acted rightly in all respects to his lord, shall not be prevented from seeking a [new] lord.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="172">III As [?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III A[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann. Liebermann compares III As 4.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
